    {
      "id": 50,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Design note: adding a provider",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 14,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 51
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Adding `provider=\"openrouter\"` (or any new provider) to this schema\n\nThe `ai:tokens:sum` / `ai:tool_calls:sum` / `ai:cost_usd:sum` recording rules\n(`provisioning/prometheus/recording-rules.yml`) are additive per provider --\na new provider needs **its own rule block per metric**, following the\nexisting `anthropic`/`openai` pattern:\n\n```yaml\n- record: ai:tokens:sum\n  labels:\n    provider: openrouter\n  expr: |\n    sum by (model, token_type, project, branch, linear_key, task_type, account, phase) (\n      <openrouter's native token-usage metric>\n    )\n```\n\n**For a new provider to show up correctly across this whole dashboard**, its\nOTLP exporter needs to emit, on whichever metric(s) carry token/cost data:\n\n| canonical label | what to stamp | notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `model` | the model id string | e.g. `glm-4.6`, `kimi-k2` |\n| `token_type` (or a label `label_replace`-able to it) | `input` / `output` / `cached` / ... | match the OpenAI/Anthropic token_type vocabulary where possible |\n| `project` / `branch` / `linear_key` / `task_type` | same `OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES` the relay dispatcher already sets for Claude/Codex | `~/catalyst/comms/coord/relay-dispatch.sh` is the one place that needs a new `--settings`/env block per provider |\n| `account` / `phase` | same dispatcher-stamped attrs | only useful once the recording rule groups by them (already done here) |\n| a REAL cost metric, if the provider bills per-token (OpenRouter does) | `<provider>_cost_usd_total` or equivalent | if real $ exist, wire a real `ai:cost_usd:sum` leg -- do NOT fall back to an estimated/list-price leg when a real number is available |\n\nOnce the metric exists with those labels, this dashboard's panels need **one\nline each**: add an `{\"expr\": ..., \"legendFormat\": \"openrouter\"}` target\nto the \"by Provider\" panels above (`Tool Calls by Provider`, `Tokens by\nProvider`, `Spend Trend by Provider`) -- the per-dimension panels\n(`Spend by Model`/`by Ticket`/`by Project`/...) don't need changes if they\nalready query the unified `ai:*` recording rule name (the `provider` label\njust gets a new value automatically).\n"
      }
    },
